      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Model Development: the model is a multilayer perceptron with one hidden layer\n",
        "class SimpleNN(nn.Module):\n",
        "    def __init__(self, input_size, hidden_size, num_classes):\n",
        "        super(SimpleNN, self).__init__()\n",
        "        self.fc1 = nn.Linear(input_size, hidden_size)\n",
        "        self.relu = nn.ReLU()\n",
        "        self.fc2 = nn.Linear(hidden_size, num_classes)\n",
        "\n",
        "    def forward(self, x):\n",
        "        out = self.fc1(x)\n",
        "        out = self.relu(out)\n",
        "        out = self.fc2(out)\n",
        "        return out\n",
        "\n",
        "# Since we are using 8x8 MNIST and flatenning the input, the input size is 8 * 8 = 64\n",
        "input_size = 8 * 8\n",
        "hidden_size = 128\n",
        "num_classes = 10 # 0-9 digits\n",
        "\n",
        "model = SimpleNN(input_size, hidden_size, num_classes)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "mnMeUXCF3dy3"
      },
      "source": [
        "**Question**:\n",
        "- The model architecture depends on the input data shape. The input images of MNIST are originally of size $28 \\times 28$ but they have been resized to $8 \\times 8$ pixels. Which changes do you need to do if you want to use the original $28 \\times 28$ size? Indicate two changes you need to do in this notebook.\n",
        "- Which change you need to do in the `SimpleNN` class if you want your model to have two hidden layers, both with size 128?\n",
        "- What is a `ReLU` activation function called by `nn.ReLU`?\n",
        "- Why are non linear activation functions like `ReLU` necessary for deep learning?"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "**Answer.**\n",
        "- To use the original `28 x 28` MNIST images, I would make two changes:\n",
        "  1. Remove `transforms.Resize((8, 8))` from the transform, or replace it with `transforms.Resize((28, 28))`.\n",
        "  2. Change `input_size = 8 * 8` to `input_size = 28 * 28`, because the flattened input vector will have length 784.\n",
        "- To use two hidden layers with size 128, the `SimpleNN` class needs one more linear layer. For example: `fc1: input_size -> 128`, `fc2: 128 -> 128`, and `fc3: 128 -> num_classes`, with `ReLU` after `fc1` and after `fc2`.\n",
        "- `nn.ReLU` applies the Rectified Linear Unit function: `ReLU(x) = max(0, x)`. Negative values become 0, and positive values stay unchanged.\n",
        "- Non-linear activation functions are necessary because they allow the network to learn non-linear patterns. Without them, several linear layers would still behave like one single linear layer, so the model would be much less powerful.\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "**Code changes for Step 2**\n",
        "\n",
        "This cell shows the required changes without replacing the current 8x8 pipeline.\n",
        "\n",
        "1. If we want to use the original 28x28 MNIST images, do not resize them to 8x8.\n",
        "```\n",
        "transform_28 = transforms.Compose([\n",
        "    transforms.ToTensor(),\n",
        "    transforms.Lambda(flatten_tensor)\n",
        "])\n",
        "```\n",
        "The flattened input size becomes 28 * 28 = 784.\n",
        "```\n",
        "input_size_28 = 28 * 28\n",
        "```\n",
        "2. A version of SimpleNN with two hidden layers, both with size 128.\n",
        "```\n",
        "class SimpleNNTwoHidden(nn.Module):\n",
        "    def __init__(self, input_size, hidden_size, num_classes):\n",
        "        super(SimpleNNTwoHidden, self).__init__()\n",
        "        self.fc1 = nn.Linear(input_size, hidden_size)\n",
        "        self.relu1 = nn.ReLU()\n",
        "        self.fc2 = nn.Linear(hidden_size, hidden_size)\n",
        "        self.relu2 = nn.ReLU()\n",
        "        self.fc3 = nn.Linear(hidden_size, num_classes)\n",
        "\n",
        "    def forward(self, x):\n",
        "        out = self.fc1(x)\n",
        "        out = self.relu1(out)\n",
        "        out = self.fc2(out)\n",
        "        out = self.relu2(out)\n",
        "        out = self.fc3(out)\n",
        "        return out\n",
        "```\n",
        "Example model for original 28x28 inputs.\n",
        "```\n",
        "model_28_two_hidden = SimpleNNTwoHidden(input_size_28, hidden_size=128, num_classes=10)\n",
        "```\n"
      ]
    },
